steps.prompt:
origin/main release check:
${steps.check_release.outputs.release}

Stage this version? Choosing 'Cancel the run' means this workflow run is cancelled (j.workflow cancel) and nothing is dispatched.

npm authentication is needed to inspect, download and approve the stage. Forward the line below to the user verbatim — if it carries a URL, they must open it and complete the login including 2FA:
${steps.npm_login_start.outputs.login}

Pick 'Waiting for sign-in' to start the ${inputs.auth_timeout_minutes}-minute wait. The next step polls npm whoami and fails the run if the sign-in has not completed in time.

ST-Test verification results for stage ${steps.stage_ready.outputs.stage_id}:
${steps.st_test.outputs.report}

How should this release proceed? 'Release to npm prod' continues into stage approve (2FA required) and then tagging. 'Already released' skips the approve attempt — the next step will report that the stage is no longer approvable, which is expected; carry on to tagging. 'Stop here' means cancel this run with j.workflow cancel and leave the stage unapproved. 'Other' means stop and ask the user what to do.
